Use beginner-friendly Python 3.10+ and the standard library.
Use clear snake_case names and short function docstrings.
Preserve the task requirements before refactoring.
Validate factorial and Fibonacci inputs; reject negatives.
Explain bugs and changes in simple English.
Use unittest for normal, boundary and invalid-input cases.
Never invent execution results or submission status.
Run python -m unittest discover -s tests -v after changes.
